WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.500
Couple things to get you started.

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.560
While nutrition is an
important consideration here,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.050
I need to make sure that
it's completely clear here.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:11.130
Resistance exercise is by
far the greater stimuli

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.010
of muscle growth relative to nutrition.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.090
Really from this perspective,

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.610
we need to make sure we
have sufficient calories,

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.130
which is to be said as hyper caloric.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.960
So we need a little bit more
calories and we're burning.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.160
Does this stay alive?

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.560
And mostly we need to
focus on protein here.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.630
1.6 grams per kilogram

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.460
of body weight is a great place to start.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.920
Now I personally prefer
a little bit higher,

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.850
2.2 grams per kilogram, which
is about one gram per pound.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.190
But actually I believe the
science is pretty clear here.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.870
Suggesting that going from 1.6

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.330
to 2.2 is not really going
to increase the amount

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.190
of muscle you're you're growing.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.260
And if it is, it's not
going to be by much.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.990
And so, if you prefer to
be at 1.6, that's fine.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.450
Higher is absolutely okay as well

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.820
and it may aid in some
people in some circumstances.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.980
But going below 1.6 seems

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.710
to reduce the amount
of muscle you can grow.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.510
So we want to be at least that number.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.310
From a training perspective,

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:05.640
you want to start by focusing
on your big muscle groups.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.320
Now if you have a particular muscle

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.270
or group of muscles that
you want to increase

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:12.570
for any number of reasons, say
you've identified assymetry,

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:15.210
have a personal preference,
you enjoy that more,

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.460
you just want to have a
muscle group grow larger

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.920
for some aesthetic reasons,
that's absolutely fine.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.090
Focus on those.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.000
But you really shouldn't
omit everything else either.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.090
It's critically important
to maintain posture

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.530
and joint integrity

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.710
by ensuring we have adequate
muscle surrounding each joint.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:33.240
Which basically means we need

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.480
to address each muscle at some
point throughout the week.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.610
We can certainly emphasize
some more than others.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.350
That's no problem whatsoever.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.910
But we don't want to leave big chunks

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.880
of muscles completely unchallenged.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.932
That's going to present
problems more likely if not now,

00:01:47.932 --> 00:01:49.023
down the road.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.320
So we also want to challenge these muscles

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.160
across multiple stimuli,
meaning exercises.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.850
So whether you prefer your body
weight, machines, dumbbells,

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:03.180
kettlebells, or any number
of other strategies,

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:04.410
those are absolutely fine.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:05.970
All are incredibly effective.

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:07.470
And at the highest level,

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.690
it actually doesn't
really matter that much

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.940
which of those strategies you try,

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.080
because at the end of the day

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.450
it's just about stimulating the muscle.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.460
However you go about
that is absolutely fine.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.500
So you have lots of options there.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.050
Perhaps in a future episode
we'll get into the the details

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:24.570
and spend the entire discussion
on that going over pros

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.450
and cons of those different
strategies and tactics.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:30.000
But for now at at again
the most zoomed out level,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.950
you've got a tremendous amount of options

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:36.480
regarding which exercise
you select and which modes

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.260
and methodologies you do to
engage that resistance exercise.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.060
The range of motion is critical.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.680
You want to use the largest range

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.390
of motion you can while still being safe

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.210
and protective of both
the exercising joint

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:51.030
as well as the joint
above it and below it.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.620
So an example here,

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.280
let's just say you're interested
in growing your quadriceps.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.740
You want to have a lot of
activity over both the knee

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.870
and hip joint, but you want to make sure

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.490
that you're doing though that in a case

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.800
in which you're not
compromising your low back

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.060
and say your feet.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.400
And so making sure we're
protecting the joints above

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.803
and below the muscle group
is important as well.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.950
So we really want to challenge our muscles

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.890
as much as we can in a
variety of ways there.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:20.940
In terms of how much to
do the repetitions per set

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.650
doesn't really matter,

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:25.200
such that you can have success
in a number of them anywhere

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.930
between, say as low as
five repetitions per set,

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.360
all the way up to 30 or
more repetitions per set

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.450
can be equally effective
for muscle growth.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:34.740
The total amount of sets per week

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.510
is probably the bigger determinant.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.550
From there, you probably want
to be in the neighborhood

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:43.470
of about 15 to 20 working
sets per muscle per week.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:44.880
If you were to break that down,

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.860
let's say you were focusing again

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.510
on your hamstrings muscles,

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:51.720
if you did three sets on day one,

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:52.950
three sets on day two

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.110
and three sets on day three,

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:58.620
that would give you a total
of nine working sets per week.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.840
That's probably a little bit too low.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.470
But if you did two hamstring
exercises each day,

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:07.050
three sets each, that'd
be six sets day one,

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.240
six sets day two, six sets day three,

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.200
and now you're up to close

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.720
the 18 working sets per per week rather.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:14.790
That's a pretty good spot to be in.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.890
Lots of things we could
talk about there in terms

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:18.210
of advanced athletes and elite,

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.770
but structurally

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:22.110
and roughly that's going
to put you in the ballpark.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.370
That's going to be enough stimulus

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.170
for most people to grow most of the time.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.120
Last consideration here is frequency,

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.550
as I sort of alluded to
here, somewhere between two

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:32.310
to three days per week per
muscle group is a great way

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.660
to go about it.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.630
More is fine as well if you
can handle the recovery.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.300
Less than two days a week is
also theoretically possible.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.190
There's excellent research
showing one day a week

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.190
per muscle group is sufficient
in muscle to grow muscle.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.990
It does become practically
challenging though,

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:46.920
because now you've got to fit

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.200
all those working sets into a single day.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.570
And that is challenging both
in the length of the workout

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:55.980
as well as how sore and
how much damage you create.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.190
So what I recommend here is
what I call the 72 hour rule,

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.110
which is every seven two hours

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.080
or so work each of your muscles

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.060
to a nice pump or contraction.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:09.000
Remember, we want to
stimulate muscle growth here,

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.400
but we don't want to
annihilate the muscle either.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.970
Excessive fatigue and damage
and soreness does not aid

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:18.180
in muscle growth and can
actually harm our ability

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.460
to come back and train
again in the next session,

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:21.990
or even the one following that,

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.630
which would then reduce
our overall total volume.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:28.470
So enough intensity, enough
difficulty to stimulate growth,

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.846
but not so much that we
completely annihilate it.

00:05:30.846 --> 00:05:34.050
We got to be able to repeat
that every 72 hours or so.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.480
So, again the way I say
it, take it to a nice pump,

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.880
a nice contraction,
whatever that means to you.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.110
And that's going to get a lot of people

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:43.023
in a close enough ballpark
to growing muscle.

00:05:43.023 --> 00:05:45.508
[music]

